<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: FlyDubai suspends flights to and from Israel after pilot attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1353032529ac7b7a6efc91e3972d31668a6d77cf09af29e75878bf742da2ed9</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T05:58:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-live-flydubai-suspends-flights-to-and-from-israel-after-pilot-attack--44a1c7b6f345.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-live-flydubai-suspends-flights-to-and-from-israel-after-pilot-attack" /><summary type="html">FlyDubai, the budget airline owned by Emirates Airlines, has temporarily suspended flights to and from Israel after one of its pilot stabbed his copilot midflight in what appears to have been an attempt to crash the Tel Aviv-bound passenger yet. Israel’s defence minister has labelled the incident as a thwarted “terror attack”. Follow our liveblog for all the latest developments.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Like a 'rollercoaster': passengers describe harrowing flydubai flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e34a173269ef0f07d5b8807523615b7f253837c6a536e636a3b8831a375ef756</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T21:31:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/like-a-rollercoaster-passengers-describe-harrowing-flydubai-flight--9d7009b2f605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/like-a-rollercoaster-passengers-describe-harrowing-flydubai-flight" /><summary type="html">As flight FZ 1073 from Dubai to Tel Aviv approached the Jordanian border on Wednesday, passengers knew in an instant that something was wrong when the plane began plummeting from the sky in a rapid dive. It was like "we were having very big turbulence, but there was no turbulence", passenger Almog Italie told AFP, describing the sensation of losing thousands of feet of altitude in seconds as similar to riding a "rollercoaster". FRANCE 24's August Hakansson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Attempted terror attack’: What happened on board the rerouted Flydubai flight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df49f0fc63230cb228c7fcd6d0be0a8991107cc5218023ee122da67aa3469e5c</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:04:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attempted-terror-attack-what-happened-on-board-the-rerouted-flydubai-flight--427fdbaf19b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attempted-terror-attack-what-happened-on-board-the-rerouted-flydubai-flight" /><summary type="html">The co-pilot of a flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv ​tried ‌to crash the plane after stabbing the pilot, but passengers then ⁠held him down while other pilots landed the plane safely in Saudi Arabia, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said ‌on Wednesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mixed reactions in Iraq on final day of US-led coalition withdrawal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:976247efce50b857036fffb444c501a41942911013e25042feff0a4c9a43442d</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T11:27:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-mixed-reactions-in-iraq-on-final-day-of-us-led-coalition-withdrawal--29152cc8659b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-mixed-reactions-in-iraq-on-final-day-of-us-led-coalition-withdrawal" /><summary type="html">The US military announced on Wednesday that it has completed the withdrawal of all American troops from Iraq, ending a 12-year mission to fight the Islamic State group. The last US troops left an air base in northern Iraq under a deal between Baghdad and Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu says Israel is preparing for other ‘potential threats’ after pilot tried to crash plane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f85a33e4a840a7a7add567810e6d33cb3037f90ee4b9d01c91fde8aa0667ccd</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:25:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-israel-bound-flight-diverted-to-saudi-arabia-after-brawl-between-pilots--5eb43950f821.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-israel-bound-flight-diverted-to-saudi-arabia-after-brawl-between-pilots" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said that one of the pilots of an Israel-bound flight had tried to kill the other and crash the plane, but that passengers and crew had managed to overpower him and safely land the plane in Saudi Arabia. All the passengers have since arrived in Israel, and Saudi authorities have arrested and are interrogating the alleged assailant.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US forces leave Iraq, raising fears of Iran-backed militias amid power vacuum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5fe316183436b57f6442f42c34ce999d08acd46734151a9d09cfa21466088af</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T01:04:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-us-forces-leave-iraq-raising-fears-of-iran-backed-militias-amid-power-vacuum--6f5d6f0a7ff6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-us-forces-leave-iraq-raising-fears-of-iran-backed-militias-amid-power-vacuum" /><summary type="html">US forces are withdrawing from their remaining bases in Iraq on Wednesday, completing a pullout agreed under former president Joe Biden as fears grow over the security vacuum it could leave. Iraqi officials and analysts warn the departure could embolden Iran-backed militias and give Islamic State group fighters room to rebuild their capabilities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Settler raid on West Bank village injures Israeli forces, drawing rare government rebuke</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c88d3c27e79ee4047416487f33be44ef29c71ca9e61a84b7397a0322dc02b57</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-settler-raid-on-west-bank-village-injures-israeli-forces-drawing-rare-government-rebuke--5c1887db9a8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-settler-raid-on-west-bank-village-injures-israeli-forces-drawing-rare-government-rebuke" /><summary type="html">More than 100 Israeli settlers stormed a village in the occupied West Bank early on Tuesday, setting fire to Palestinian properties and wounding three members of Israel's security forces. The raid, which drew rare government condemnation, came as the military attempted to accompany a Palestinian family back to their home after they had been displaced by earlier settler attacks.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Video shows Iranian police beating, sexually humiliating teenage detainee</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be47783fd9f5630914d762615fa0cb2a502030b05301185f9818dc10a3718d03</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T09:56:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-police-video-teenage-detainee-abuse--3fd5b34486fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-police-video-teenage-detainee-abuse" /><summary type="html">A video posted in mid-September showing Iranian police officers beating and sexually harassing an arrested teenage boy has caused widespread outrage in Iran. Experts say such mistreatment of people accused of common crimes is frequent in Iran, but the footage provides rare visual evidence of what they describe as a recurring practice within the police force.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran says it expects US response Tuesday on plan to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:151c6c8d59bcf8c45c4a2235746b5da475211fff44f82171f26dc44e52d0e793</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T06:32:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-says-expects-us-response-tuesday-plan-reopen-strait-of-hormuz--63f87509ea04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-says-expects-us-response-tuesday-plan-reopen-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said Tehran expects Washington to respond to its proposal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz on Tuesday. In exchange for reopening the vital shipping route, Tehran is seeking guarantees including a regional ceasefire, the lifting of sanctions on its oil sector and an end to the US naval blockade.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump 'flips &amp; flops' with Iran between making a deal and threats to attack in ‘devastating fashion’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10e1113a23f72555a468a97bb54a09f3bca3309d48f5391f97d021f047468051</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T18:18:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260928-saudis-furious-trump-flips-flops-between-deal-with-iran-and-attacks-in-devastating-fashion--c70fe6067205.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260928-saudis-furious-trump-flips-flops-between-deal-with-iran-and-attacks-in-devastating-fashion" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Stimson Center. She describes the US-Iran conflict as a dangerous combination of military escalation, diplomatic ambiguity and political calculation. Slavin sees an absence of true diplomacy: the recent indirect contacts between Washington and Tehran, mediated by Qatar, have been too limited and too fragile to produce any serious breakthrough. For her, this amounts to "kabuki diplomacy": they half engage while positioning themselves against any appearance of compromise.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Trump expects Iran talks next week after rejecting seven-day truce proposal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81f98408228f2190af5c11c5d4ec6c72fc3c87b40e16aed6a99f2eb640b84e0d</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T22:10:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-trump-expects-iran-talks-next-week-after-rejecting-seven-day-truce-proposal--ec7a283e05ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-trump-expects-iran-talks-next-week-after-rejecting-seven-day-truce-proposal" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday said he expected talks with Iran to resume next week, despite rejecting Tehran’s proposal for a seven-day truce followed by the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz. Trump raised the possibility of renewed air strikes on Iran but also said he anticipated further negotiations.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel revokes Dutch diplomats' West Bank credentials over settlement goods ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79bd1039cc04d89769f1e6fdd0d101e346ee5fa2a4a183d5d4c5d2ab61b85121</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T21:47:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-israel-revokes-dutch-diplomats-credentials-settlement-sanctions--c9e6069f5a47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-israel-revokes-dutch-diplomats-credentials-settlement-sanctions" /><summary type="html">Israel will revoke the diplomatic accreditation of Dutch officials based in the occupied West Bank after the Netherlands began enforcing a ban on goods from Israeli settlements, Foreign Minister Gideon Saar said Sunday. The officials have seven days to surrender their Israeli-issued diplomatic papers, he added.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East: Palestinians plan first local elections in 20 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0229787872157a3748f25374d5a729d38da1197e3bff0fdaf25434f41bf731e1</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T12:29:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-palestinians-plan-first-local-elections-in-20-years--211e8e3008fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-palestinians-plan-first-local-elections-in-20-years" /><summary type="html">Oliver McTernan, Director and co-founder of Foward Thinking in London, is our guest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East: An art centre for children in occupied West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7202c85f1999ff36c11892e29d4b36e72f6464b00cd47a31ebde8595d88791a5</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T10:10:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-an-art-centre-for-children-in-occupied-west-bank--a778dd857aa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-an-art-centre-for-children-in-occupied-west-bank" /><summary type="html">To help children process their experiences of war, an art center has been established in the West Bank.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East: Iran proposes Hormuz plan, Donald Trump reportedly refuses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7e45f8146eccab2a9121682d08a527d776bf52d0cd7a531da357334f1c08f73</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T09:35:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-iran-proposes-hormuz-plan-donald-trump-reportedly-refuses--0c236672cf1a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-iran-proposes-hormuz-plan-donald-trump-reportedly-refuses" /><summary type="html">The United States had yet to publicly respond on Saturday after Iran offered a plan to reopen the strategic Strait of Hormuz, though reports indicated that President Donald Trump had rejected the proposal. The waterway key to the world's oil supply is central to the conflict between the US and Iran, which is at a stalemate after nearly seven months, though new mediation efforts took place this week.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israelis, Palestinians must 'reboot relations': Absence of diplomatic route means 'perpetual war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94d3f513c1cdddd4aa89fb5b18000f85212ed32e2d4ac3cd2d5abe92c5616799</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T07:50:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israelis-palestinians-must-reboot-relations-absence-of-diplomatic-route-means-perpetual-war--a967accb3eb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israelis-palestinians-must-reboot-relations-absence-of-diplomatic-route-means-perpetual-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Yossi Mekelberg, Senior Consulting Fellow of the Middle East and North Africa Programme at Chatham House. Can Israel continue to define its future primarily through security and territorial control? Mekelberg challenges the notion that military operations, incursions and settlement expansion can constitute a sustainable political objective. He identifies a potential transition beyond the Netanyahu era as an opportunity to reconsider the relationship between Israeli and Palestinian societies. His central argument is that the continuation of war without a political endgame risks a state of perpetual conflict.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump rejects Iran’s seven-day plan to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e1be49ecc8ff2bb304bc2ec4f4c6fee58d1900072a23fc4b6c962724b648299</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T02:06:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260926-trump-reportedly-rejects-iran-s-7-day-plan-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz--f4edda057a7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260926-trump-reportedly-rejects-iran-s-7-day-plan-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday rejected an Iranian plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz. Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi presented the proposal to Trump’s envoy Steve Witkoff a day earlier on the sidelines of a UN gathering in New York. The plan stipulated that the important waterway would reopen seven days after an agreement was reached.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's president calls on his people to mobilise against Iran-backed Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9571710d00e8f93e0070de217dd2fdf53d4546242293518011e0a89797403222</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T20:41:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260925-yemen-president-calls-on-his-people-to-mobilise-against-iran-backed-houthis--89065aa49aef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260925-yemen-president-calls-on-his-people-to-mobilise-against-iran-backed-houthis" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Riyadh-based President Rashid al-Alimi on Friday called on ‌his people to mobilise and join the armed ‌forces while offering a general amnesty to the Iran-backed Houthi rebels who have seized swaths of Yemen's Red Sea coast and imposed a naval blockade on Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'Iran has dragged us into this conflict,' top Emirati diplomat Anwar Gargash says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e4d00860e9449d78452d6023a9b1afd9c68b9ab8d4ca559132a2a32340c54fa</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:04:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260925-iran-has-dragged-us-into-this-conflict-top-emirati-diplomat-anwar-gargash-says--f3e23abd416a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260925-iran-has-dragged-us-into-this-conflict-top-emirati-diplomat-anwar-gargash-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24 on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly, Anwar Gargash, senior diplomatic adviser to the UAE president, said Iran "has dragged us into this conflict", after the UAE was "the target of 3,300 missiles and drones" fired by Iran. After US President Donald Trump said he could either negotiate with or "obliterate" Iran, Gargash warned that the "current situation of no war, no peace is not sustainable".</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Macron says ‘military resources’ to be sent to Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dc2cb04165ac4bef2c90d4a0c327f55de8e2264a097cbeb01f1f498c937baff</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:04:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/macron-says-military-resources-to-be-sent-to-saudi-arabia--23b178d3533f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/macron-says-military-resources-to-be-sent-to-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">Speaking to broadcasters TF1 and France 2, French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday announced that “military resources” will be sent to protect the Yanbu oil site in Saudi Arabia, integral to maintaining the kingdom’s fuel exports and increasingly threatened by Yemen’s Iran-backed Houthi rebels.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tehran offers US seven-day plan to open Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96a750a0676d4b37b053abbba2879742d0417e11b2d553660ff348aceed1d64b</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T23:52:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-live-iran-s-president-says-us-must-choose-whether-to-end-war--8669e9479fa5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-live-iran-s-president-says-us-must-choose-whether-to-end-war" /><summary type="html">Iran on Friday offered the United States a seven-day plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz to maritime navigation. Initial word of a possible offer to lift the naval blockade emerged from the sidelines of the UN General Assembly earlier in the day. Read our liveblog to see how the day’s events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi reports fresh Houthi attacks as France pledges to defend key oil port</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7894f99557bfb1e895b3353a3489578dfb50de178edd0764989460da10af5eda</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T23:34:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-saudi-houthi-attacks-france-oil-port--b181320ddfb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-saudi-houthi-attacks-france-oil-port" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia intercepted Houthi ballistic missiles on Thursday after warning several regions, including Mecca, of possible attacks. France said it would send military assets to help protect the Saudi oil terminal at Yanbu. The strikes came amid renewed fighting in Yemen that has killed dozens, according to sources cited by AFP.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli PM Netanyahu calls Gaza genocide allegations ‘biggest lie of the century’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3adec96a7bc60848dc433e25cc8dc619434d6130d116d1fecea4ec78a9d2ca1c</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:31:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-israel-must-win-because-we-ve-got-no-other-choice-pm-netanyahu-tells-un--515acad11225.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-israel-must-win-because-we-ve-got-no-other-choice-pm-netanyahu-tells-un" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu gave a combative speech at the UN General Assembly on Thursday in which he denied that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza, lashed out at leaders, including New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani, and said attacking Iran was "one of the easiest decisions" he had ever made.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Residents in West Bank's Masafer Yatta face Israeli demolitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa8d5a2d3364e7ceb34a94487dd9451c909705600146302512aa853c3cf122e8</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:47:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-residents-west-bank-masafer-yatta-israeli-demolitions--70cf9dfea7fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-residents-west-bank-masafer-yatta-israeli-demolitions" /><summary type="html">On September 2, the Israeli army demolished the village of Khirbet a-Taban in the occupied West Bank. The village is located in Masafer Yatta, an area Israel declared a restricted military zone. Residents of the area have been reporting an increase in demolitions by the Israeli army and harassment by Israeli settlers since the October 7 Hamas attack.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>US war on Iran: Trump will 'declare victory and go home', embracing the 'Greenland option'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84f9d33e9c52733e4168e41b4be672d5b5f3f01a5419c2832f6da80a833afb3a</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T02:35:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260924-us-war-on-iran-trump-will-declare-victory-and-go-home-embracing-the-greenland-option--6a5dcb3c91e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260924-us-war-on-iran-trump-will-declare-victory-and-go-home-embracing-the-greenland-option" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes Scott Anderson, journalist, war correspondent and best-selling author of "King of Kings: The Fall of the Shah and the Revolution That Forged Modern Iran". For Anderson, there is a striking parallel between 1979 and 2026: Washington's persistent misreading of Iran, and the consequences that follow.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey to hand over military base in northern Iraq to Baghdad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f4925459e0b3ae810cd2c19d8d16e5f35a9bb936927f3549bd76bdf8c0a993b</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T00:02:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-turkey-to-hand-over-military-base-in-northern-iraq-to-baghdad--46f25e037ab4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-turkey-to-hand-over-military-base-in-northern-iraq-to-baghdad" /><summary type="html">Turkey will gradually hand over control of its Bashiqa military base in northern Iraq to Baghdad, Ankara and Baghdad said Wednesday, in a move aimed at strengthening Iraqi state authority and easing a long-running source of tension between the neighbours.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran will 'never bend at the knee', Pezeshkian tells UN in defiant wartime address</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a985a3991bdc1d51cb359f9b17795f9f592be0df0272a5766e1c8fa2dc55c05</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:49:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address--10f22d78db02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian gave a defiant wartime address at the UN on Wednesday accusing the US of terrorism in his country and saying Iran would not "bend at the knee". But as Pezeshkian called for diplomacy, Iranian officials downplayed their talks with US counterparts on the sidelines of the gerenal assembly as "not anything new".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01bf8aec8e53034808878769d919ba86f2c15a69ac12103e7a47a40208ae8e5a</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism--68195566b037.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has hit back at US President Donald Trump’s speech in his address to the UN General Assembly. He opened by showing images of Iranian civilians killed in US strikes, saying they demonstrated the impact of US and Israeli military action against Iran. During his speech, the US delegation walked out of the General Assembly hall. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Iranian President Pezeshkian adresses UNGA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9bd4c94da86cf57582bb441ad4399a2bfdee8dfc9e5bdecb33fdd898ba1ff120</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:44:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1--ba655932baa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".</summary></entry><entry><title>Golan Heights will 'remain Syrian', President Ahmed al-Sharaa vows at UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:159c6d7563bfc9e7de98caac1fa5b399e31c4f57620e7812071bdfe935c5f718</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:31:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-golan-heights-will-remain-syrian-president-al-sharaa-vows-to-un--f84fe9f69d85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-golan-heights-will-remain-syrian-president-al-sharaa-vows-to-un" /><summary type="html">Syria's President Ahmed al-Sharaa told the UN Wednesday that the contested Golan Heights region would "remain Syrian" despite ongoing military occupation by Israel. The Syrian leader also used his second turn at the UN rostrum to denounce repeated Israeli strikes on his country.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
